what are the major critical issues that you resolved in pipeline deployments ????

We deployed a new version of a Python FastAPI ML application to AKS.
Immediately after deployment:
Users were getting: 503 Service Unavailable

Investigation
kubectl get pods
CrashLoopBackOff
kubectl logs pod-name
ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'sklearn'
Developer had added a new dependency but forgot to update:  requirements.txt

Resolution
Updated:requirements.txt 
Added:scikit-learn
Pipeline rebuilt Docker image.
Deployed new image.

What I Learned
Added validation in Jenkins pipeline:pip install -r requirements.txt
This prevented missing dependency issues in future releases.

One critical issue I faced was a production deployment failure where Python application pods entered CrashLoopBackOff state after deployment.
I checked pod logs and identified a missing Python dependency which was not included in requirements.txt. 
After updating dependencies and rebuilding the Docker image, the application recovered successfully.
To avoid recurrence, I implemented dependency validation during Jenkins CI stages.


